## Symptom

Inflating any CustomResourceDefinition whose schema uses `items` â that is, any
CRD with an array field, so nearly every real one â dies:

```
Can't locate IO/K8s/ApiextensionsApiserver/Pkg/Apis/Apiextensions/V1/JSONSchemaPropsOrArray.pm
in @INC ... at Module/Runtime.pm line 120.
```

Reproduced against 1.105 with a minimal CRD (one `type: array` property):

```perl
use IO::K8s;
my $crd = {
  apiVersion => 'apiextensions.k8s.io/v1', kind => 'CustomResourceDefinition',
  metadata => { name => 'widgets.example.com' },
  spec => { group => 'example.com', scope => 'Namespaced',
    names => { plural => 'widgets', kind => 'Widget' },
    versions => [{ name => 'v1', served => \1, storage => \1,
      schema => { openAPIV3Schema => { type => 'object', properties => {
        spec => { type => 'object', properties => {
          tags => { type => 'array', items => { type => 'string' } } } } } } } }] },
};
IO::K8s->new->struct_to_object(
  'IO::K8s::ApiextensionsApiserver::Pkg::Apis::Apiextensions::V1::CustomResourceDefinition', $crd);
# -> dies as above
```

## Cause

`JSONSchemaProps.pm` declares four attributes whose types are classes that the
distribution does not ship:

| line | attribute | declared type |
|---|---|---|
| 10 | `additionalItems` | `Apiextensions::V1::JSONSchemaPropsOrBool` |
| 12 | `additionalProperties` | `Apiextensions::V1::JSONSchemaPropsOrBool` |
| 23 | `dependencies` | `Apiextensions::V1::JSONSchemaPropsOrStringArray` |
| 42 | `items` | `Apiextensions::V1::JSONSchemaPropsOrArray` |

`ls lib/IO/K8s/ApiextensionsApiserver/Pkg/Apis/Apiextensions/V1/` shows only
`JSONSchemaProps.pm` â none of the three `JSONSchemaPropsOr*` classes exist, in
the released 1.105 or in the repo. The declaration is only resolved when the
attribute is actually populated, which is why this stayed hidden: a CRD without
arrays or `additionalProperties` inflates fine.

## What these three types are upstream

All three are Kubernetes' union types, and each needs a hand-written inflator
rather than a plain generated class â that is likely why they were skipped:

- **JSONSchemaPropsOrArray** â either a single JSONSchemaProps, or an array of
  them. (`items: {...}` vs `items: [{...},{...}]`)
- **JSONSchemaPropsOrBool** â either a JSONSchemaProps or a plain boolean.
  (`additionalProperties: false` vs `additionalProperties: {...}`)
- **JSONSchemaPropsOrStringArray** â either a JSONSchemaProps or an array of
  strings.

In the Kubernetes OpenAPI spec these serialise as the bare alternative, not as a
tagged wrapper â so round-tripping has to preserve which arm was used, and
`false` must not collapse into an empty object.

## Impact

Anything that reads CRDs back as typed objects. Found from OCP, where every
`ocp apply` prints this to stderr while installing Gateway API and NFD CRDs. It
is currently swallowed by an `eval`, so the run completes, but CRDs cannot be
handled as typed objects at all.

## Suggested direction

Add the three classes with inflate/deflate that keeps the union arms apart, and
a round-trip test per arm â single vs array `items`, boolean vs schema
`additionalProperties`, string-array vs schema `dependencies`. A CRD fixture
with all four attributes populated would have caught this at build time; worth
adding regardless of how the types get implemented.

