## Update: it is four classes, not three, and it is a hard blocker

A second run hit a different one first:

```
Can't locate IO/K8s/ApiextensionsApiserver/Pkg/Apis/Apiextensions/V1/JSON.pm
```

Scanning the shipped V1 directory for types that existing classes reference but
that are not present gives the complete list:

| missing class | referenced by shipped code |
|---|---|
| `JSON` | 3x |
| `JSONSchemaPropsOrBool` | 2x |
| `JSONSchemaPropsOrArray` | 1x |
| `JSONSchemaPropsOrStringArray` | 1x |

`JSON` is the fourth: upstream `apiextensions.k8s.io/v1.JSON` is the
free-form value used by `default`, `example` and `enum` entries in a CRD
schema. Like the other three it has no fixed shape — it holds whatever the CRD
author wrote — so it also needs a hand-written inflator rather than a generated
class.

Which of the four you hit first depends only on which field the CRD happens to
use, so fixing them one at a time just moves the error.

## Severity is higher than first reported

The original report said the failure is swallowed by an `eval` on the OCP side
and the run completes. That was true of the path OCP hit at the time. On a
clean bootstrap it is not: `ocp apply` dies in its CRD step with a non-zero
exit, so a cluster cannot be brought up at all while this is open. Any consumer
that reads or writes CustomResourceDefinitions as typed objects is blocked, not
merely noisy.
## Fixed on branch fix/apiextensions-union-types (commit f7f393f)

All four classes added: JSON, JSONSchemaPropsOrArray, JSONSchemaPropsOrBool,
JSONSchemaPropsOrStringArray. The core change is a single line in
struct_to_object: a class providing a FROM_STRUCT class method takes over its
own inflation completely and owns its TO_JSON in return. struct_to_object is
the sole funnel for is_object, is_array_of_objects and is_hash_of_objects, so
one hook covers all seven affected attributes rather than special-casing four
class names in the core.

Verified: the exact repro from this ticket inflates and round-trips, with
additionalProperties: false staying false instead of collapsing to {}.
t/31_apiextensions_unions.t adds 14 subtests / 71 assertions covering each arm
in both directions, the empty-array arms, all three boolean input encodings
(JSON::PP::Boolean, \1 and \0 scalar refs, plain YAML::PP scalars), absence of
internal arm names in output, and byte-identical round-tripping of a CRD using
all four types. Full suite: 34 files, 1156 tests, PASS.

